Accept a declared meet of two unrelated classifiers

`Setup.checkClassifiedInheritance` rejected any class whose base classes
include two unrelated classifiers, even when another classifier among
them derives from both. That classifier is their meet, and
`CaptureOps.classifier` (the `leastClassifier` fold over the base
classes) already picks it as the least classifier; the fold collapses
to `Nothing` only when no such meet exists. The check now accepts an
unrelated pair when a declared meet is present, so a capability can be
classified by, say, a `Durable` classifier and a level-exempt one at
once.

